x86_64-linux  cxx1 names a static local `count.s` where Itanium spells it _ZZ5countiE1s - docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "A static local keeps its own name in the object file" - and its guard `count.s.guard` where clang writes _ZGVZ5countiE1s; the same object under two names. And clang names __cxa_guard_abort, the call its landing pad makes if the constructor throws while the guard is held: cxx1 emits no such pad, which docs/CONFORMANCE.md records under "A static local's guard is not released if its constructor throws"
x86_64-windows  the same static locals, which cxx1 spells its own way and clang ?s@?1??count@@YAHH@Z@4US@@A, and their guards, which clang names ?$TSS0@?1??count@@YAHH@Z@4HA; and _Init_thread_abort, the Microsoft twin of __cxa_guard_abort above - the pad that would call it is not emitted
arm64-darwin  ___cxa_guard_abort alone: the guard the Itanium ABI wants released if a static local's constructor throws, and the landing pad cxx1 does not emit - docs/CONFORMANCE.md
